.\" Man page for elled(8)
.\" Generated for ELLE 0.1.0
.TH ELLED 8 "January 2025" "ELLE 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
elled \- ELLE daemon for telemetry and privileged operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B elled
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B elled
is the daemon component of ELLE, providing:
.IP \(bu 2
Telemetry ingestion from systemd journal, kernel, and probes
.IP \(bu 2
Man Vault indexing (SQLite+FTS5 search of man pages)
.IP \(bu 2
Incident Vault for decision memory and pattern matching
.IP \(bu 2
OpenAI-compatible REST API endpoint
.IP \(bu 2
Polkit helper for privilege escalation
.IP \(bu 2
eBPF telemetry collection (when capabilities permit)
.PP
The daemon runs as a systemd service under the \fBelle\fR user account
with minimal privileges and strict security hardening.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Use specified configuration file instead of defaults.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-journal
Disable systemd journal monitoring.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-api
Disable REST API endpoint.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is loaded from (in order of precedence):
.IP 1. 3
Command-line options
.IP 2.
Environment variables (prefix: ELLE_)
.IP 3.
/etc/elle/elle.toml
.IP 4.
Built-in defaults
.SS Key Configuration Options
.TP
.B daemon.db_path
Path to main event database. Default: /var/lib/elle/elle.db
.TP
.B daemon.api.enabled
Enable REST API. Default: true
.TP
.B daemon.api.host
API bind address. Default: 127.0.0.1
.TP
.B daemon.api.port
API port. Default: 8377
.TP
.B daemon.probes.memory_interval
Memory probe interval in seconds. Default: 30
.TP
.B daemon.probes.disk_interval
Disk probe interval in seconds. Default: 300
.SH CAPABILITIES
When running with eBPF telemetry enabled, the daemon requires:
.TP
.B CAP_BPF
Load/unload BPF programs and create maps (kernel 5.8+).
.TP
.B CAP_PERFMON
Attach to tracepoints and perf events (kernel 5.8+).
.TP
.B CAP_NET_ADMIN
Network namespace access for network probes (optional).
.PP
These capabilities are granted through the systemd unit file using
AmbientCapabilities.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/elle/elle.db
Main telemetry event database.
.TP
.I /var/lib/elle/manvault.db
Man page full-text search index.
.TP
.I /var/lib/elle/incidents.db
Incident vault for decision memory.
.TP
.I /var/lib/elle/reactive.db
Reactive function definitions.
.TP
.I /var/lib/elle/policy.db
Policy engine rules.
.TP
.I /var/lib/elle/backups/
Configuration backup directory.
.TP
.I /etc/elle/elle.toml
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/elle/environment
Environment file for systemd.
.TP
.I /lib/systemd/system/elled.service
Systemd unit file.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/com.elle.policy
Polkit policy definitions.
.SH SECURITY
.B elled
implements defense-in-depth security:
.SS Privilege Separation
.IP \(bu 2
Runs as dedicated \fBelle\fR system user
.IP \(bu 2
No ambient root access
.IP \(bu 2
Polkit gates all privileged operations
.SS Systemd Hardening
.IP \(bu 2
NoNewPrivileges=true
.IP \(bu 2
ProtectSystem=strict
.IP \(bu 2
ProtectHome=true
.IP \(bu 2
PrivateTmp=true
.IP \(bu 2
ProtectKernelTunables=true
.IP \(bu 2
ProtectKernelModules=true
.IP \(bu 2
ProtectControlGroups=true
.IP \(bu 2
ReadOnlyPaths=/etc /usr /boot
.IP \(bu 2
ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/elle only
.SS Resource Limits
.IP \(bu 2
MemoryMax=512M
.IP \(bu 2
CPUWeight=50
.SH API
.B elled
provides an OpenAI-compatible REST API on the configured port
(default: 8377).
.SS Endpoints
.TP
.B GET /v1/models
List available models.
.TP
.B POST /v1/chat/completions
Chat completion endpoint (streaming supported).
.TP
.B POST /v1/embeddings
Generate embeddings via Ollama.
.TP
.B GET /health
Health check endpoint.
.TP
.B GET /events
Server-sent events for telemetry stream.
.PP
API is bound to localhost by default. Configure \fBdaemon.api.host\fR
to change binding.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start manually:
# elled
.TP
Start via systemd:
# systemctl start elled
.TP
Check status:
# systemctl status elled
.TP
View logs:
# journalctl -u elled -f
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.TP
.B "Failed to connect to Ollama"
Ensure Ollama is installed and running. Check OLLAMA_HOST configuration.
.TP
.B "Permission denied for BPF"
Kernel capabilities not granted. Check systemd unit configuration.
.TP
.B "Database locked"
Another elled instance may be running. Check for stale processes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal termination.
.TP
.B 1
Startup failure (configuration error, missing dependencies).
.TP
.B 2
Runtime error.
